<title>CHINA: HK three-yr notes average accepted yield 6.34 pct.</title>
<headline>HK three-yr notes average accepted yield 6.34 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average accepted price for three-year Exchange Fund Notes tendered on Monday was 99.55 to yield 6.34 percent, the Hong Kong Monetary Authority said.</p>
<p>The lowest price accepted was 99.40 for a yield of 6.40 percent, while the average price tendered was 99.47 for a yield of 6.37 percent, the HKMA said.</p>
<p>The notes carry a coupon of 6.08 percent and mature on July 17, 2000.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
</text>
